{"id":"a8a7ec5c-93ed-400d-8120-5d40460746a2","expr":"args != null","rationale":"It is common for the main entry point to be invoked with a non-null args array.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Main#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Main.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:50.410103Z"}
{"id":"a785cfcb-4fd8-4e1b-9566-363242213132","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"All arrays in Java have a non-negative length.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Main#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Main.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:50.410103Z"}
{"id":"d98ac2a2-37ef-4bfb-8f90-0fccdad6db61","expr":"args != null","rationale":"Main methods typically expect args to be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Main#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Main.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:50.505929Z"}
{"id":"1f1ea305-606f-4efa-9cfe-06ed3e25c073","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"Array length is always non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Main#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Main.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:50.505929Z"}
{"id":"dfc17cd5-7c38-41d9-99b0-75dda0cc0738","expr":"name != null || x == -1","rationale":"If the name is null, the method returns -1, so before normal computation x must not be -1 unless name is null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Foo#bar(int,String):int","file":"com/example/Foo.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:51.225656Z"}
{"id":"90868bc7-13a3-4736-8ca1-597a3f89a54f","expr":"name == null || name.length() >= 0","rationale":"If name is non-null, its length is at least zero.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Foo#bar(int,String):int","file":"com/example/Foo.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:51.225656Z"}
{"id":"ac57b9a3-f1f9-40cd-aad9-25bb93b569af","expr":"name != null || true","rationale":"For all inputs at method entry, name may be null or non-null (this is safe, non-trivial in some contexts as the branch is explicit in the code).","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Foo#bar(int,String):int","file":"com/example/Foo.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:51.225656Z"}
{"id":"0f2a517e-6162-4d31-a75a-57a90d82eb3f","expr":"(name == null && result == -1) || (name != null && result == x + name.length())","rationale":"Describes exactly how 'result' is determined by the state of 'name'.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Foo#bar(int,String):int","file":"com/example/Foo.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:51.711569Z"}
{"id":"52c45202-a9f6-49d1-935a-80b81bb01d35","expr":"name == null || result >= x","rationale":"If 'name' is not null, result is x + length >= x; otherwise, result could be -1 < x only if x > -1.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Foo#bar(int,String):int","file":"com/example/Foo.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:51.711569Z"}
{"id":"60a01a1a-f8d8-426e-84f0-67f210317b44","expr":"name != null || result == -1","rationale":"If name is null, result must be -1.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Foo#bar(int,String):int","file":"com/example/Foo.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:51.711569Z"}
{"id":"5bc5e04e-0dde-41e4-a17b-23d6bb6046d4","expr":"name == null || result == x + name.length()","rationale":"If name is non-null, result is always computed as x + name.length().","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Foo#bar(int,String):int","file":"com/example/Foo.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:51.711569Z"}
{"id":"818222fe-5260-47ea-aa5a-1e058734d05a","expr":"result >= -1","rationale":"Result is at least -1 for any input.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Foo#bar(int,String):int","file":"com/example/Foo.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T06:36:51.711569Z"}
